# Thrun, Breaker of Silence "can't be the target of nongreen spells your opponents control or abilities from nongreen
# sources your opponents control" (CR 601.2c, 602.2b): only while it is on the battlefield (CR 113.6), so on turn 3 Bot2's
# Counterspell targets Thrun the spell - which "can't be countered" and resolves anyway (CR 101.2). On turn 4 Bot2 can't aim
# Lightning Bolt (red) or Walking Ballista's ability (a colorless source: nongreen, CR 105.2c) at Thrun, though both are on
# offer elsewhere: the Bolt goes at Bot1 (17 life) and the Ballista's 1 damage at Bot2's own Ornithopter, which the
# restriction, naming Thrun alone, does not shield. On turn 5 Thrun attacks; Ornithopter (0/2, its damage gone in the
# cleanup step) blocks, and trample (CR 702.19b) carries 3 of Thrun's 5 damage over to Bot2.

